## IV. Application: Audio Systems
In audio systems, statistics are essential to describe and control signal properties. The **mean** detects unwanted DC offsets, while the **RMS** indicates perceived loudness, useful for normalization. The **standard deviation** reflects signal dynamics, key for compression processes. The **time average** and **quadratic mean** provide energy estimation of the signal. These measures allow efficient analysis, optimization, and processing in tasks such as mixing, equalization, noise reduction, and audio transmission.  

---

## V. Conclusion
The laboratory demonstrated the flexibility of GNU Radio to implement digital processing blocks such as accumulator, differentiator, and statistical operators. It was confirmed that statistical analysis provides powerful tools to understand signal behavior and has direct applications in fields such as audio and telecommunications. The integration of GitHub in the workflow also simulated collaborative practices widely used in the industry.  

